INSERT INTO `transfers` VALUES (85,'Hotel','Nizami Street + Hotel Drop','Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'10:00 – Leaving from Hotel to Nizami Street \n\n • One of the city’s main pedestrian streets known for shopping, cafés, and historic architecture.\n Popular walking area with boutiques, souvenir shops, and local restaurants.\n \n13:00 – Lunch Break \n \n18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)\n \n19:00 –Drop to Hotel\n \nOvernight in Baku',35.00,38.00,40.00,50.00,88.00,147.00,177.00,206.00,206.00,20.00,47.00);
INSERT INTO `transfers` VALUES (86,'Hotel','Nizami Street + Shooting range','Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'10:00 – Leaving from Hotel to Nizami Street \n\n • One of the city’s main pedestrian streets known for shopping, cafés, and historic architecture.\n Popular walking area with boutiques, souvenir shops, and local restaurants.\n \n13:00 – Lunch Break \n \n14:00 – Shooting Range\n \n- After lunch, you make your way toward the shooting range facility located within the city area, transitioning from the lively street environment to a more focused and controlled activity space.\n You will begin your shooting experience under the guidance of trained professionals who provide safety instructions and help you select appropriate equipment. The session allows you to practice target shooting in a secure indoor environment, making it an engaging and memorable activity for those looking to add excitement to their day. Whether you are a beginner or have prior experience, the range offers a structured and enjoyable session tailored to your comfort level.\n \n18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)\n \n19:00 –Drop to Hotel\n \nOvernight in Baku',35.00,38.00,40.00,50.00,88.00,147.00,177.00,206.00,206.00,20.00,47.00);
INSERT INTO `transfers` VALUES (87,'Hotel','Nizami Street + Indoor Go Karting','Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'10:00 – Leaving from Hotel to Nizami Street \n\n • One of the city’s main pedestrian streets known for shopping, cafés, and historic architecture.\n Popular walking area with boutiques, souvenir shops, and local restaurants.\n \n13:00 – Lunch Break \n \n14:00 – Indoor Go Karting Center\n \n- You begin your go-karting session inside a professionally designed track where safety briefings and equipment are provided. The experience offers fast-paced fun as you race around the track, enjoying sharp turns, competitive speeds, and a thrilling atmosphere suitable for both beginners and experienced drivers. It’s an exhilarating way to add energy and excitement to your day in Baku.\n \n18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)\n \n19:00 –Drop to Hotel\n \nOvernight in Baku',35.00,38.00,40.00,50.00,88.00,147.00,177.00,206.00,206.00,20.00,47.00);
INSERT INTO `transfers` VALUES (88,'Hotel','Nizami Street + Outdoor Go Karting','Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'10:00 – Leaving from Hotel to Nizami Street \n\n • One of the city’s main pedestrian streets known for shopping, cafés, and historic architecture.\n • Popular walking area with boutiques, souvenir shops, and local restaurants.\n\n 13:00 – Lunch Break \n\n 14:00 – Outdoor Go Karting Track\n - You begin your go-karting session on a professionally designed outdoor track where safety instructions and equipment are provided before you start. The open-air setting enhances the thrill as you race through straights and curves, feeling the excitement of competitive driving in a spacious outdoor arena. Whether you are a first-time driver or an experienced racer, the track provides an exhilarating and memorable experience that brings a burst of adrenaline to your day.\n\n 18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)\n\n 19:00 –Drop to Hotel\n\n Overnight in Baku',35.00,38.00,40.00,50.00,88.00,147.00,177.00,206.00,206.00,20.00,47.00);
INSERT INTO `transfers` VALUES (89,'Hotel','Boulevard Tour + Panaromic City Tour','Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'10:00 – Leaving Hotel to Baku Boulevard \n\n Baku boulevard tour starts along the Baku Boulevard followed by: \n - Carpet Museum \n - Mini Venice of Baku\n - Deniz Mall \n - Ferries Wheel \n - Carpet Museums\n - Cristal Hall\n\n 13:00 – Lunch Break\n\n 14:00 – Evening City Tour starts with panoramic full evening city view of Baku followed by:\n - Highland Park -Which is the highest point in the Azerbaijani capital, opening a panoramic view of the city and its bay. The city\'s residents and visitors often come here to see a bird\'s eye view of Baku, and just have a walk. The Upland Park can be reached by cable railway (funicular) in 7-8 minutes from the boulevard or by climbing up the endless stone stairs.\n - Flame Towers -The city\'s tallest building. The height of 182 m. Flame Towers - consisting of three high-rise buildings in the complex.\n\n 18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)\n\n 19:00 –Drop to Hotel\n\n Overnight in Baku',35.00,38.00,40.00,50.00,88.00,147.00,177.00,206.00,206.00,20.00,47.00);
INSERT INTO `transfers` VALUES (90,'Hotel','Boulevard Tour + Heydar Aliyev Centre','Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'10:00 – Leaving Hotel to Baku Boulevard \n\n Baku boulevard tour starts along the Baku Boulevard followed by: \n - Carpet Museum \n - Mini Venice of Baku\n - Deniz Mall \n - Ferries Wheel \n - Carpet Museums\n - Cristal Hall\n\n 13:00 – Lunch Break\n\n 14:00 – Visit to Heydar Aliyev Center & “I LOVE BAKU” sign Photostop\n - If it’s first time of your arrival to Baku, just be aware of that \n from the bird view you can clearly see the Heydar Aliyev’s \n Signature on the Heydar Aliyev’s Center design. It’s a wave-like\n building rises from a bed of concrete. Its immobile white walls \n look as though they have been frozen mid-ripple. The abstract \n architecture is unlike anything else in the capital city. The \n Heydar Aliyev Center, which was designed by renowned architect Zaha Hadid\n\n 18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)\n\n 19:00 –Drop to Hotel\n\n Overnight in Baku',35.00,38.00,40.00,50.00,88.00,147.00,177.00,206.00,206.00,20.00,47.00);
